.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-cert-issue 1  "ngx-cert-issue " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-cert\-issue \- Obtain a Let\*(Aqs Encrypt certificate for a site and switch it to HTTPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-cert\-issue\fR [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-staging\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-credentials\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Obtain a Let\*(Aqs Encrypt certificate for a site and switch it to HTTPS
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Email for the Let\*(Aqs Encrypt account (if none exists yet)
.TP
\fB\-\-staging\fR
Use the Let\*(Aqs Encrypt staging server
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\fR \fI<PLUGIN>\fR
Use the DNS challenge with this certbot DNS plugin (e.g. cloudflare): wildcards, no port 80 needed
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-credentials\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Credentials file for the DNS plugin (e.g. /root/.secrets/cloudflare.ini, mode 600)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID or domain
.SH EXTRA
ngx\-created sites use the ACME webroot (certbot certonly \-\-webroot); other sites use certbot\*(Aqs nginx plugin (certbot \-\-nginx).

Example:
  sudo ngx cert issue 5 \-\-email me@example.com
